  "body": "### Description\n\nContrary to what the [docs](https://matrix-org.github.io/synapse/latest/admin_api/user_admin_api.html#list-accounts) say, the \"List Accounts\" Admin API endpoint will always return `next_token`.\r\n\r\nAffected code seems to be\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/86b7d9b8862775353951322d604624e37d428a55/synapse/rest/admin/users.py#L143-L146\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Have more than 100 users\r\n- Fetch users with query `next_token=100`\r\n- Watch the result contain `next_token: 100`\r\n\n\n### Homeserver\n\nlocal dev\n\n### Synapse Version\n\nv1.70.0\n\n### Installation Method\n\nDocker (matrixdotorg/synapse)\n\n### Platform\n\nDebian\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nsynapse.access.http.8008 - 450 - INFO - GET-13505- 10.250.250.5 - 8008 - {<snip>} Processed request: 0.002sec/0.001sec (0.001sec, 0.000sec                                                                                                                                                     ) (0.000sec/0.001sec/2) 27206B 200 \"GET /_synapse/admin/v2/users?order_by=admin&dir=b&next_token=100 HTTP/1.1\" \"-\" [0 dbevts]\n```\n\n\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\n\n_No response_",
